WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.850
Now let’s set it.

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.525
Do it the same way every time.

3
00:00:04.775 --> 00:00:12.900
Choose your spot: good holding bottom, shelter from the wind you expect, and room to swing a full circle without hitting anything.

4
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:18.700
Head slowly into the wind or current, whichever is stronger, and stop over the spot.

5
00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:21.125
Lower the anchor to the bottom.

6
00:00:21.375 --> 00:00:23.150
Never throw it.

7
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.950
Why not?

8
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:30.625
A thrown anchor lands in a pile of its own rode and fouls itself.

9
00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:35.275
Let the boat drift back, or back down slowly, as you pay out your scope.

10
00:00:35.525 --> 00:00:40.225
Then snub the line, let the anchor bite, and set it with gentle reverse.

11
00:00:40.475 --> 00:00:42.550
And you’re still not finished.

12
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.175
Take bearings on two landmarks, or set a GPS anchor alarm.

13
00:00:47.425 --> 00:00:50.175
That’s how you’ll know if she starts to move.
